            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospitalisation of your 67-year-old female patient, admitted on 29/08/2024 due to an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Diagnostic workup included chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, pulse oximetry, and blood tests, confirming an infective exacerbation without pneumonia. Spirometry supported significant airflow obstruction. She was treated with inhaled bronchodilators via nebuliser, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and intravenous fluids. Clinical response was satisfactory with improvement in oxygenation and symptom relief. She was discharged on 30/08/2024 in stable condition. Please continue maintenance inhaler therapy and arrange outpatient pulmonary follow-up. Patient education regarding exacerbation management and smoking cessation was provided prior to discharge.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
